1+ year of work experience as B2B Account manager in IT or/and IGaming industry;
Analytical mindset;
Highly developed social and communication skills;
Ability to cope with a high-pace, complex and changing environment;
Strong drive for achieving and exceeding targets;
Desire to learn and to research;
To work as a team member;
Experience with Jira/CRM/Google;
Knowledge of English;
Fluent English — spoken and written.
Your position will include
Act as the main point of contact and develop a trusted advisor relationship with existing customers;
Ensure games launch, marketing and promotional activities across brands;
Problem resolution of technical/management/financial/business issues on a regular basis;
Attend and represent the company at events and exhibitions;
Provide Account Team Lead with monthly / quarterly reports on the work results;
Conducting a regular analysis of the iGaming market.

We’re here to make a difference! The iGaming world is fun. It’s an exciting and fast-changing industry, and we provide people with different services for their consistent growth, wellness and fun.
20 paid working days of annual leave;
12 paid sick days;
An additional day off on your birthday;
Access to a corporate psychologist to support your mental well-being;
Remote and hybrid work options;
Flexible working hours;
A strong culture of volunteering and social responsibility, with opportunities to join and organize charitable initiatives;
Internal mobility program to explore new roles and career paths.
If you are ready to work in a dynamic team, passionate about the product, technology, and the world of entertainment, we’re waiting for your CV and portfolio to schedule an online/offline meeting and get to know each other better!
Your CV will be carefully reviewed by our TA department, and if it meets the requirements of the position, we will contact you within 3 business days to discuss the possibility of scheduling an interview.
